v _ {\mathrm{s}} ^ {2} = \frac {k (T _ {\mathrm{e}} + T _ {\mathrm{p}})}{m _ {\mathrm{p}}}. $$ Accordingly, the disk half-thickness is $$
H = \left(\frac {2 k \left[ T _ {\mathrm{e}} + T _ {\mathrm{p}} \right] R ^ {3}}{G M m _ {\mathrm{p}}}\right) ^ {1 / 2} \simeq 3. 2 m _ {*} r ^ {3 / 2} k T _ {*} ^ {1 / 2} \mathrm{km}, \tag {A3}
